  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of molecules from the following which contain only two lone pair of electrons is _____________</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>CO</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>NO</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The lone pair of electrons can be identified by drawing structure of the given moleules as follows,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ebad69fe-d331-4134-a59f-5fcd08e46f71.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 526px;\" /></p><p>The number of molecules having only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> lone pair of electrons&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Which are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math>.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;lone pairs&nbsp;on central atom, but we are asked about lone pair in molecule</p>",
